# Normalize to LF in the repository and on checkout, regardless of a contributor's own
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# converts tracked text files (including .rs sources) to CRLF on disk; a multi-line raw
# string literal (e.g. install/rule.rs's RULE_BODY) then embeds whatever line ending was
# physically in the source file at compile time, silently producing CRLF output on
# Windows builds and making local test runs diverge from what's actually committed (LF)
# and what CI (Linux) checks out and sees.
* text=auto eol=lf
